  "verbalization": "Phytolaccoside B is shown to have a target relationship with multiple downstream proteins, including mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 13, Serine/threonine-protein kinase MARK1, and Serine/threonine-protein kinase ULK2. These proteins are all part of a signaling pathway that leads to the activation of Chymotrypsin-like elastase family member 2A. The evidence suggests that Phytolaccoside B may modulate this pathway, potentially influencing the activity of Chymotrypsin-like elastase family member 2A. The scores from the three paths indicate a consistent level of confidence in the relationship, with final scores of 0.6514, 0.6397, and 0.6397, respectively. The shared involvement of a common intermediate compound, (1S,2S,5R,6R,7S,8S,11S)-7-hydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)-11-[(2R)-1-hydroxypropan-2-yl]-6-methyl-9-oxatricyclo[6.2.1.02,6]undecan-10-one, supports the notion that Phytolaccoside B acts through a shared mechanism to influence the activity of Chymotrypsin-like elastase family member 2A. The evidence is consistent and suggests a plausible biological relationship, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the functional significance of this interaction."
